Package: agern
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Agern developers <https://github.com/Egernet-CS/agern/issues>
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: default-jre-headless (>= 2:1.17) | java17-runtime-headless, git, ca-certificates, curl, passwd
Recommends: postgresql
Suggests: gh, podman (>= 4.3), uidmap, netavark, aardvark-dns, crun, slirp4netns
Homepage: https://github.com/Egernet-CS/agern
Description: Agern - the software factory
 A self-hosted web system where people put Claude agents to work building
 software. A GitHub organization is the source of truth: repositories are
 projects and issues are tasks. Agents are 'claude' CLI processes started by
 the server as the unprivileged 'agern' user.
 .
 Needs a PostgreSQL database ('agern setup-db' creates one on a local
 PostgreSQL), the 'claude' CLI and 'gh' for the agern user ('agern doctor'
 says what is missing). Optional build/test sandboxes in rootless Podman are
 off until 'agern sandbox enable' (which says what to install). See
 /usr/share/doc/agern/README.Debian.
